  <prompt>
    Implement FR-08 (version-stamp + re-anchor-on-stale). Version-stamp EVERY save with the SPE eTag + the
    projection schema version; assert the stamp before applying the operation log. If the base has MOVED
    (the persisted eTag/schema-version no longer matches the load-time stamp), do NOT fail with an eTag 500
    — instead RE-ANCHOR the operation log via `Services/Compose/AnnotationReanchorService.cs`: the AUTO band
    applies confident re-anchors; REVIEW + ORPHAN results SURFACE for review (never silently dropped). Only a
    genuinely un-re-anchorable operation becomes an ORPHAN that surfaces — no operation is ever silently lost.

    Modify `Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs` (the save path). Re-anchor/version summary state (NOT the
    document bytes) is cached via `IDistributedCache` per ADR-009 — MUST NOT use `IMemoryCache`. Reuse
    `AnnotationReanchorService.cs` (a KEEP asset) as the fuzzy re-anchor layer — do NOT reimplement bands.
    The SPE hop stays behind `SpeFileStore` (ADR-007) — no `Microsoft.Graph` type in `Services/Compose/`.
    `Services/Compose/` stays pure (ADR-013 Tier-1 NetArchTest green). Every save/load change carries a
    through-the-wire seam slice (ADR-038; the concurrency seam slice is task 054).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior .NET 8 engineer on `ComposeService` + the SPE facade write + the Open XML operation applier.
    Understands that Word regenerates paraIds on external tracked-change saves (design D2 / §5.6 pitfall),
    so a stale base must re-anchor via fuzzy bands rather than fail — and that no operation is ever silently
    dropped (the AnnotationReanchorService contract).
  </role>

  <goal>
    A save path where every save is version-stamped (SPE eTag + projection schema version) and asserted before
    apply; a stale base RE-ANCHORS the operation log via `AnnotationReanchorService` (AUTO applies, REVIEW/ORPHAN
    surface) instead of throwing an eTag 500; and an un-re-anchorable operation surfaces as an ORPHAN, never
    silently dropped. Re-anchor/version summary state uses `IDistributedCache` (not `IMemoryCache`); the SPE hop
    stays behind `SpeFileStore`; `Services/Compose/` stays pure.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §5 (save + concurrency): "version-stamp every save (SPE eTag + projection schema version); assert
      before applying; if the base moved, re-anchor the op log via `AnnotationReanchorService` (AUTO apply /
      REVIEW+ORPHAN surface) instead of failing." Design D2 + §5.6 pitfall: Word regenerates paraIds on external
      tracked-change saves, so `AnnotationReanchorService` fuzzy match is the cross-Word-session / stale-base
      fallback (a MUST rule in spec). This task depends on 032 (both legacy writers retired; the unified Patch
      Engine is the sole write path) so re-anchoring targets one applier. The eTag-sequencing for create-on-save
      (051) and the HTTP 423 lock protocol (052) build on this same save path.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs — the save path: version-stamp (SPE eTag + projection schema version); assert before apply; re-anchor the op log on a stale base via AnnotationReanchorService instead of failing</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/AnnotationReanchorService.cs — KEEP asset: fuzzy re-anchor bands (AUTO/REVIEW/ORPHAN) + ambiguity guard + never-silently-drop; REUSE as the stale-base / cross-Word-session fallback</file>
      <file role="dependency-output">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeShadowPatchEngine.cs — task 030/032 unified Patch Engine (the sole write path the re-anchored op log applies through)</file>
      <file role="dependency">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/SpeFileStore.cs — SPE eTag read/write stays behind this facade (ADR-007)</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/design.md §5 (save + concurrency), D2, §5.6 pitfall</file>
      <file role="spec">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/spec.md FR-08, NFR-08</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="032" status="pending">Both legacy writers retired; the unified `ComposeShadowPatchEngine` is the sole write path re-anchored operations apply through.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-08">Every save MUST be version-stamped (SPE eTag + projection schema version) and asserted before applying the op log. A stale base MUST re-anchor via `AnnotationReanchorService` (AUTO apply / REVIEW+ORPHAN surface) INSTEAD of failing with an eTag 500.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec / NFR-08 / project">An un-re-anchorable operation MUST surface as an ORPHAN — NEVER silently dropped and NEVER silently placed. Reuse `AnnotationReanchorService` bands; MUST NOT reimplement or fork them.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-009 / project">Re-anchor/version SUMMARY state (not the document bytes) is cached via `IDistributedCache` — MUST NOT use `IMemoryCache`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007 / NFR-05">The SPE eTag read/write stays behind `SpeFileStore` — no `Microsoft.Graph` type in `Services/Compose/`. The applier is `byte[]`-in/`byte[]`-out.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013 / NFR-05">`Services/Compose/` injects NO AI internals; Tier-1 NetArchTest stays green.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 / NFR-06">Through-the-wire seam slice required for this save-path change (authored as the task 054 concurrency seam slice). NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration, or ctor-null tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10 / project">State the Placement Justification (save/re-anchor orchestration stays in `Services/Compose/`; reuses `SaveAsync`/`SpeFileStore`/`AnnotationReanchorService` seams). Verify BFF publish size ≤60 MB compressed, report absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB (incl. PDBs). No new HIGH CVE. Run `/conflict-check` before the PR.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Version-stamped save; stale-base re-anchor via AnnotationReanchorService bands; Redis-first summary state (IDistributedCache); SPE facade eTag; BFF hygiene</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-007-spefilestore.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-009-redis-caching.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-010-di-minimalism.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Fuzzy re-anchor bands + never-silently-drop" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/AnnotationReanchorService.cs">
        AUTO applies a confident re-anchor; REVIEW/ORPHAN surface; ambiguity guard refuses to auto-place; nothing is silently dropped — reuse as the stale-base / cross-Word-session re-anchor fallback.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="SPE facade eTag read/write" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/SpeFileStore.cs">
        Read the load-time eTag and write with an atomic If-Match — keep the Graph hop behind this facade; the save path sees only `byte[]` + version tokens.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor (bff-api + docx + spe; xhigh; sonnet). Load the knowledge files + bff-extensions.md + design §5. Read `ComposeService.cs` save path + `AnnotationReanchorService.cs` bands. State the Placement Justification. Run `/conflict-check`.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Version-stamp the save">Stamp every save with the SPE eTag + the projection schema version; persist the summary stamp via `IDistributedCache` (ADR-009, not `IMemoryCache`). Assert the stamp before applying the operation log.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Re-anchor on stale base">When the persisted eTag/schema-version no longer matches the load-time stamp, re-anchor the operation log via `AnnotationReanchorService`: AUTO band applies; REVIEW/ORPHAN results are collected to surface. Do NOT throw an eTag 500.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Surface ORPHANs, never drop">Ensure an un-re-anchorable op becomes an ORPHAN that surfaces for review — never silently dropped or placed. Apply the re-anchored + AUTO ops through the unified Patch Engine; write via the SPE `If-Match` path.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Verify + size/CVE report">`dotnet build`; run existing `Services/Compose` unit tests + Tier-1 NetArchTest. Publish; report absolute size + delta vs ~49.63 MB; `dotnet list package --vulnerable`. (The through-the-wire concurrency seam slice is task 054.)</step>
    <step order="5" name="Index + deviations">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅. Document any deviation (esp. the cross-Word-session paraId regen boundary if it fired) in projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>The cross-Word-session paraId REGENERATION boundary — if a stale base cannot be re-anchored because Word regenerated the paraIds wholesale on an external tracked-change save, and the fuzzy bands cannot confidently re-anchor a material fraction of the op log, STOP and escalate per root §6 rather than surfacing a document as mostly-ORPHAN silently. This is a known judgment boundary (design D2 / §5.6), not a case to improvise past.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs (version-stamp + assert + re-anchor-on-stale)</output>
    <output type="report">Placement Justification; publish-size absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB; CVE scan; `/conflict-check` result for the PR</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">Every save is version-stamped (SPE eTag + projection schema version) and the stamp is asserted before applying the operation log; the summary stamp is cached via `IDistributedCache` (not `IMemoryCache`).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A stale-base save RE-ANCHORS the operation log via `AnnotationReanchorService` and completes WITHOUT an eTag 500; AUTO-band re-anchors apply and REVIEW/ORPHAN results surface.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: an un-re-anchorable operation surfaces as an ORPHAN (surfaced for review) — it is NEVER silently dropped and NEVER silently placed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The SPE eTag read/write stays behind `SpeFileStore` (no `Microsoft.Graph` in `Services/Compose/`, ADR-007); `Services/Compose/` injects no AI internals (Tier-1 NetArchTest green, ADR-013); `AnnotationReanchorService` is reused, not reimplemented.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish size reported absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB, ≤60 MB; no new HIGH CVE; `dotnet build` + existing Compose tests green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    The through-the-wire proof (stale-base save re-anchors, no eTag 500) is authored as the task 054 seam
    slice under `tests/integration/seam/Compose/`. 051 (eTag sequencing) and 052 (HTTP 423 lock) extend this
    same save path. Run `/conflict-check` before the BFF PR (`Services/Compose/` overlaps sibling projects).
  </notes>

